From 7ea9c8387213317a2ad58551518b85a60632221c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:55:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] hw/sensor: add an AP3216C ambient light / proximity /
 IR sensor model

Minimal teaching model for boards carrying an AP3216C on i2c1 @ 0x1e
(the AES i.MX6ULL board). Register-index + auto-increment access
following the datasheet; the six read-only data registers (0x0a..0x0f)
are derived from three injectable ir/als/ps uint16 QOM properties, so a
classroom 'flashlight' is a QMP qom-set away. Bit layout matches the
Linux driver's parsing: IR 10-bit with IR_L[1:0] holding the top two
bits, ALS plain 16-bit LE, PS 10-bit with PS_L[3:0] holding the top
nibble. The overflow/invalid flag bits are never set.

The mcimx6ul-evk machine attaches one at 0x1e on i2c1 by default
(via the SoC's s->i2c[0].bus, since QEMU 11's qdev_get_child_bus no
longer accepts NULL for 'first bus').

Verified on mcimx6ul-evk + Linux v7.1: i2cget -y 0 0x1e 0x0c w returns
the injected ALS value 0x0120.
